## A streamlined .gitignore for modern .NET projects
## including temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular .NET tools. If you are
## developing with Visual Studio, the VS .gitignore
## https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/VisualStudio.gitignore
## has more thorough IDE-specific entries.
##
## Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Dotnet.gitignore

.vs/
# VS Code: share the build and debug configuration, keep personal state out.
# Must be ".vscode/*" and not ".vscode/" - git will not descend into an ignored
# directory, so the negations below would never be considered.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
bin/
obj/
Flowcharts/.*

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# .NET Core
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# ASP.NET Scaffolding
ScaffoldingReadMe.txt

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg

# Others
~$*
*~
CodeCoverage/

# MSBuild Binary and Structured Log
*.binlog

# MSTest test Results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*

# NUnit
*.VisualState.xml
TestResult.xml
nunit-*.xml

# Stop-hook marker: fingerprint of the last verified-green test run
.claude/.tests-green

# Webserver content
Assets/Webserver/

# Stop-hook state stamps (local, per-clone)
.claude/.tests-green
.claude/.wiki-reminded

# Server configuration that can hold credentials (Phase 3 onward).
#
# The deployed service reads appsettings.Production.json from its own directory on the server
# (see DEPLOYMENT.md), which lives OUTSIDE this repository and is never copied into it. These
# patterns exist for the local-development
# case: a file created here by accident, or an appsettings.Development.json written while
# testing against a tunnelled database, would otherwise be a connection string in git history.
#
# "appsettings.Example.json" is deliberately NOT ignored - it is committed, with placeholder
# values only, so the shape of the real file is documented. Keep real values out of it.
#
# Local development uses "dotnet user-secrets", which stores outside the repository tree
# entirely; see src/CRT.Server/DEPLOYMENT.md.
src/CRT.Server/appsettings.Production.json
src/CRT.Server/appsettings.Development.json
src/CRT.Server/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.Production.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
*.pfx

# The framework-dependent publish output for the server, produced by the dotnet publish line in
# DEPLOYMENT.md step 4 and copied to the box by hand. Build output, not source - and it carries a
# copy of whatever appsettings files were present when it ran.
publish-server/
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# Scratch folders holding a lone "p.csx", created by an editor "run this snippet"
# action rather than by anything in this project. Two of them ("aggfield", "castchk")
# were created a day apart under unpredictable names, and one had already been
# committed by accident, so the pattern is ignored rather than the two names: a third
# would otherwise arrive under a name nobody thought to list. Nothing here is built or
# referenced - .csx is not picked up by the SDK "**/*.cs" compile glob either.
p.csx
